<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-COLLATED WORLD CUP SOCCER SOUTH AMERICAN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COLLATED WORLD CUP SOCCER SOUTH AMERICAN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of</p>
<p>South American World Cup qualifying matches played Wednesday.</p>
<p>In Quito: Ecuador 0 Colombia 1 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Faustino Asprilla (72nd minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 45,000</p>
<p>In Asuncion: Paraguay 2 Chile 1 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Paraguay - Carlos Gamarra (24th), Catalino Rivarola (63rd)</p>
<p>Chile - Javier Margas (22nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>In San Cristobal, Venezuela: Venezuela 2 Argentina 5 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Venezuela - Gabriel Savarese (7th), Rafael Dudamel (87th)</p>
<p>Argentina - Ariel Ortega (35th), Juan Sorin (69th), Diego</p>
<p>Simeone (77th), Jose Albornoz (90th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Played Tuesday:</p>
<p>In Montevideo: Uruguay 1 Bolivia 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Juan Manuel Pena, own goal (62nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabuluate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Colombia    5  4  1  0 10  3 13</p>
<p> Ecuador     5  3  0  2  8  6  9</p>
<p> Argentina   5  2  2  1  9  6  8</p>
<p> Paraguay    4  2  1  1  5  3  7</p>
<p> Uruguay     4  2  0  2  4  5  6</p>
<p> Bolivia     4  1  1  2  7  5  4</p>
<p> Chile	 4  1  1  2  7  8  4</p>
<p> Peru	  4  0  3  1  2  5  3</p>
<p> Venezuela   5  0  1  4  4 15  1</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders. matches:</p>
<p>Next matches: November 10 - Paraguay v Ecuador, Peru v</p>
<p>Venezuela, Bolivia v Colombia, Chile v Uruguay.</p>
